WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.340
Here are the guide's Step 6 commands.

2
00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:08.035
Create the firewall policy in alert mode,
on Premium, from Learn's C L I reference.

3
00:00:08.035 --> 00:00:13.095
Route each workload subnet's default
route, zero dot zero dot zero dot zero

4
00:00:13.095 --> 00:00:18.072
slash zero, to the firewall's private
I P, with Learn's route table commands.

5
00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:20.047
Send the logs to the workspace.

6
00:00:20.047 --> 00:00:24.502
Leave threat intelligence and intrusion
detection in alert for two weeks,

7
00:00:24.502 --> 00:00:27.524
reading their logs for hits
on legitimate traffic.

8
00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:29.774
Then move to deny through a draft,

9
00:00:29.774 --> 00:00:34.273
so every change lands at once and
can be reviewed: create the draft,

10
00:00:34.273 --> 00:00:38.683
update both modes to Deny, show it,
and deploy it in a change window.

11
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:41.805
Learn's page, Azure Firewall
Draft plus Deployment,

12
00:00:41.805 --> 00:00:44.482
carries one warning
that the guide repeats:

13
00:00:44.482 --> 00:00:48.868
deploying replaces the whole applied
policy, so changes made to the live

14
00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:53.403
policy after the draft was created are
lost unless they're in the draft too.

15
00:00:53.403 --> 00:00:55.978
Keep one change path, drafts only.

16
00:00:55.978 --> 00:00:58.387
And east-west, as design guidance:

17
00:00:58.387 --> 00:01:03.530
spoke to spoke through the hub firewall,
with N S Gs denying by default.
